    prov:value "[{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"content\": \"Now we have weather and facts. Next, we need to transfer to writer with what they found. The instruction: \\\"Then transfer to the writer with what they found.\\\" So we should call transfer_to_agent with agent_name \\\"writer\\\", presumably providing the gathered info. But the transfer function only takes agent_name; no payload. However we might need to include the data in the transfer? The function signature: transfer_to_agent{agent_name: string}. It likely just transfers control; maybe the writer will get the context from the conversation. So we just call transfer_to_agent.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"id\": \"call-bd229585-7c21-4f64-9d4b-f947563ad337\", \"name\": \"transfer_to_agent\", \"arguments\": {\"agent_name\": \"writer\"}, \"type\": \"tool_call\"}], \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}]" ;
